# The functions without a body the lint can follow that allocate nothing, or that only a bug reaches (design item 17),
# by path; an entry ending in `::` names every function under that path. Each line gives its reason.

alloc::alloc::__rust_dealloc	frees memory, never allocates
core::panicking::	a panic runs only on a bug, and a panic while unwinding aborts whatever it would allocate
std::panicking::	a panic runs only on a bug, and a panic while unwinding aborts whatever it would allocate
std::rt::	the runtime's panic entry points, as above
core::intrinsics::	compiler intrinsics, which allocate nothing
virtual_drop::Closer::close	the case's trait method, whose implementations the lint checks as roots
core::slice::index::slice_index_fail	a slice index out of range panics, which runs only on a bug, and a panic while unwinding aborts whatever it would allocate
